#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""pi-doctor — daily self-healing audit for every project on the Pi.

Checks each project end-to-end and applies SAFE automatic fixes; anything
not safely fixable is escalated to the owner (WhatsApp + ntfy) with the
evidence. Layered with (not replacing) the faster watchers:

  loop-heartbeat  ...  every 30 min: dead-man + service up/down + healthz
  deploy timers   ...  every 5 min:  code rollout + health gate + rollback
  pi-doctor       ...  daily:        deep audit + repair + report

Per-project checks:
  1. service active + not flapping (start/stop churn)
  2. HTTP healthz/UI reachable (where the project serves one)
  3. deploy pipeline: running commit == origin/main HEAD (drift = the
     5-min deploy timer is broken)
  4. CI on origin/main is green
  5. git tree clean (no mystery local edits)

Deliberate states are reported, never "fixed":
  * units stopped by `ram-mode focus` (owner park) -> left stopped, listed
  * ais-catcher idling while a NOAA capture owns the RTL-SDR -> left alone

Safe fixes applied automatically:
  F1 service dead/not-found-but-unit-exists -> systemctl reset-failed + start
  F2 deploy drift (running != HEAD)         -> run deploy.sh once
  F3 CI failed on main                      -> nothing (report only; a human
                                               decides revert vs fix-forward)

System checks: disk %, CPU temp, memory, rpi-connect leak, AdGuard DNS,
failed units, loop-heartbeat/doctor state health.

Output: human report; exit 0 always (never breaks cron). Alerts only on
actionable findings; all-green runs are silent except --verbose.
"""
